  "tour": "2026 Summer Tour",
  "notes": "<p>This show was Phish's 93rd performance at Madison Square Garden and featured a setlist composed entirely of songs from the 1993 era of the band, Trey wearing a Marvin the Martian T-shirt (a common occurrence in 1993), and multiple bustouts: Big Ball Jam (last played <a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-december-09-1994-mesa-amphitheatre-mesa-az-usa.html\">December 9, 1994</a>, or 1,170 shows), La Grange (last played <a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-july-08-2012-saratoga-performing-arts-center-saratoga-springs-ny-usa.html\">July 8, 2012</a>, or 531 shows), Sparks (last played <a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-december-30-2016-madison-square-garden-new-york-ny-usa.html\">December 30, 2016</a>, or 357 shows), Makisupa Policeman (last played <a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-july-11-2023-orion-amphitheater-huntsville-al-usa.html\">July 11, 2023</a>, or 149 shows), Kung (last played <a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-november-30-2019-dunkin-donuts-center-providence-ri-usa.html\">November 30, 2019</a>, or 258 shows), and Sweet Adeline (last played <a href=\"https://phish.net/setlists/phish-december-29-2016-madison-square-garden-new-york-ny-usa.html\">December 29, 2016</a>, or 358 shows). Trey teased I Can't Turn You Loose in Bathtub Gin. Weigh's lyrics were changed to \"on a summer day.\" Makisupa included the lyrics \"iced green matcha tea, policeman looking at me\" lyrics. Kung began over the Makisupa drumbeat. Trey quoted <a href=\"https://phish.net/song/big-balls\">Big Balls</a> in the Tube prior to Big Ball Jam.</p>",
  "permalink": "https://phish.net/setlists/phish-july-24-2026-madison-square-garden-new-york-ny-usa.html",
